            {
              "id": "392bdf01-d648-4290-995a-49427fc92c98",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Traditional &amp; Folk Puppets of the World</strong></em> was written by Michael R. Malkin, published by A. S. Barnes, January 1, 1977."
            },
            {
              "id": "e1fd7142-20c8-4e3a-a0d7-37fd8f19f586",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "c0b48a4a-869e-47ca-9fe4-96c290bbc324",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>For many, puppets belong to childhood memories using tangled strings and one's imagination...This book adds facts to those recollections showing that for thousands of years puppetry has been a traditional and highly developed form of entertainment for the wealthy, aristocratic elite, or as folk theater. Great images and information to enjoy is presented in a pleasant way, so read up and enjoy!</em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "6c529276-9ce2-4b68-89df-7b7a4cb02715",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
